# Curating annotations

Curators review the annotations submitted by all annotators for an article, to
produce a single, authoritative annotation.

## Opening the curation view

Navigate to **Curation Queue** in the sidebar. Each article shows how many
annotators have submitted their work. Click on an article to open the curation view.

## Reviewing entities and entity mentions

The curation view shows the list of entities that have been annotated for the current document.
Entities marked as "proposed" are not yet part of the project's knowledge graph and need to be
reviewed for inclusion.

Clicking on a entity opens a list of all the mentions that have been annotated for it in the current text and highlights those mentions in the text itself, which is shown on the right.
If you click on a list item, the corresponding highlight will be focused on the text, and vice-versa: if you click on a highlight, its corresponding list item will be focused.

You can edit each mention or remove it. If you don't do anything, the mention is automatically accepted when you save the curated annotation.  

## Finalising

Once you are satisfied with the curated annotation, save it. The article is then
marked as curated and removed from the active queue.
